-complex surfaces with compact exceptional locus. For each
-$\mathcal R\in\{C^0,C^2,C^\infty\}$, $X$ admits a psh exhaustion of
-class $\mathcal R$ if and only if $X'$ does.
-\end{proposition}
-\begin{proof}
